+## One libtorch per process (important)
+namd3 itself NEEDs libtorch_cpu/libc10 (colvars torchann, `-DCOLVARS_TORCH`) and
+is linked `-rdynamic`, so inline torch symbols compiled into namd3 interpose the
+shim's.  namd3 and the shim MUST be built against the same libtorch.  On
+2026-09-21 `Linux-x86_64-g++/Make.config` TORCHDIR was switched to
+libtorch-2.11.0+cu130, `obj/colvarcomp_torchann.o` rebuilt and namd3 relinked
+(backups: `namd3.libtorch2.6.bak`, `Make.config.libtorch2.6.bak`,
+`obj/colvarcomp_torchann.o.libtorch2.6.bak`).  Symptom of a mismatch:
+"set_stride is not allowed on a Tensor created from .data or .detach()" in
+mlff_eval_batch.  At run time LD_LIBRARY_PATH (namd_benchmarks/env.sh,
+LIBTORCH_ROOT) picks the copy namd3 and the shim share.
+
+## Custom-op libraries: NAMD_MLFF_EXTRA_LIBS
+Colon-separated list of .so paths.  mlff_load() dlopen's each one
+`RTLD_NOW|RTLD_GLOBAL`, in order, before `torch::jit::load`, so TorchScript
+custom ops (cuEquivariance, TorchANI cuAEV, vesin-torch, OpenEquivariance, ...)
+are registered when the archive is deserialized.  Before that it promotes the
+already-loaded libtorch libraries to global scope (RTLD_NOLOAD) because NAMD
+loads the shim RTLD_LOCAL.  A failing dlopen makes mlff_load fail with
+"NAMD_MLFF_EXTRA_LIBS: dlopen(<path>) failed: <dlerror>".  List dependencies
+first (e.g. libcue_ops.so before the cuequivariance torch extension).
+
+## Exit-time teardown
+mlff_free() leaks the model once the process is exiting (atexit hook armed on
+the first eval).  With libtorch 2.11, freeing CUDA tensors from NAMD's
+atexit(cleanupMLFFThread) ran after libtorch's CUDA statics were gone and
+aborted finished runs ("Unrecognized stream ...").
+
 Produces `$OUT/libnamd_mlff.so`. The cxx11 ABI is auto-detected from libtorch.
 
